docs {
  # GET /api/pricing/?location=&vehicle=&service_type= — Filtered pricing

  Same as `get_list.bru` but with optional filters via `DjangoFilterBackend` (`travels/views.py:36`, `filterset_fields=["location","vehicle","service_type"]`). Each query param is optional; combine any subset. Requires `Authorization: Token {{token}}`.

  ## Status codes

  - `200 OK` — success (filtered)
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/invalid token

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "count": 1,
    "next": null,
    "previous": null,
    "results": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "location": { "id": 1, "name": "Alegranza" },
        "vehicle": { "id": 1, "name": "Luxury SUV", "passengers": 4 },
        "service_type": { "id": 1, "name": "One Way" },
        "price": 80.0
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Filter is exact by PK (`?location=1&vehicle=1&service_type=1` → 1 row for Alegranza + Lux SUV + One Way). Use `One Way=1, Round Trip=2` per fixtures.

  ## Error (401)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "Invalid token.",
    "data": {}
  }
  ```
}
